  "text": "Cú Roí grounds the account of the captive Bláthnat. The poet Fercheirtne, who served Cú Roí, pushed Bláthnat over a cliff. Fercheirtne died in the very same act. Bláthnat had been held as a slave by Cú Roí. Later retellings often call her a traitor. They blame her for plotting his death. A Christian legend offers a softer end. In that version she turns to the faith and joins a convent instead of being killed.",
